            <ArticleTitle>[Central nervous system tumor: an unusual etiology for limb pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1465-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Limb pain in children is one of the most frequent reasons to refer to the emergency unit. Most often it suggests an orthopaedic, a muscular, a peripheral neurologic or a spinal affection. We report two cases of recurrent limb pains revealing a central nervous system tumor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
